{"type": "tool_defect", "tool": "design-check.js contrast", "severity": "medium", "summary": "Resolves a colour token to its LAST occurrence in the file, so a document writing two themes as two tables has one theme silently unmeasured and the other measured.", "detected": "2026-10-02, on .forge/design/design-system.md", "impact": "With day and night as two tables, `contrast` measured night only; `tokens-used` then reported the design system's own day table as 18 offenders 'valeur_differe_de_celle_du_design_system' - the file disagreeing with itself.", "workaround": "One row per token with Day and Night as separate columns. `contrast` reads the first column, so Day is now machine-verified and Night is not.", "residual_risk": "The Night column is not machine-checked. Its ratios were computed with the same WCAG formula and are recorded in the document, and the gap is disclosed there rather than left implied.", "ts": "2026-10-02T15:42:04.282559Z"}
{"type": "tool_defect", "tool": "design-check.js contrast", "severity": "low", "summary": "A token declared `on:` a background it is never actually drawn on is measured there and reported as a real contrast offender.", "detected": "2026-10-02, on .forge/design/design-system.md", "impact": "`--color-text-inverse` was listed `on: --color-surface-raised`, producing an 'offender' of 1.17:1 describing a text-on-surface combination the app never renders.", "workaround": "The `on:` list now contains only the accent and semantic fills. An `on:` entry that is not true is not neutral - it manufactures a false failure that looks real.", "residual_risk": "none", "ts": "2026-10-02T15:42:04.282631Z"}
