{"type": "process_error", "tool": "state.js", "severity": "low", "summary": "There is no `unregister` command, so a deliverable registered by mistake cannot be removed through the tool.", "detected": "2026-10-02, while registering the first screen file", "detail": "Screens belong in state.screens via `register <anchor> screen <key> <path>`. I first used `register ... deliverable ...`, which created a second registry entry pointing at the same file. Both now track the same hash and all guards pass, so the duplicate is cosmetic -- but it means every edit to that file must re-register TWICE or `content_hashes_current` and `no_content_drift` fail.", "fix": "Register screens with kind=screen. If a deliverable entry was created by mistake, re-register it after every edit rather than trying to delete it.", "tool_defect": "`state.js hash <root> <key>` with an extra `deliverable` segment silently prints state instead of hashing; the documented fix for a drifted screen hash is `register`, not `hash`.", "ts": "2026-10-02T15:53:54.698397Z"}
